# A fixed-capacity first-in, first-out buffer of values of type `T`.
#
# Add the fields you need. The buffer owns its values: `write` and `overwrite`
# move a value in, `read` moves the oldest one back out.
#
# The errors are the strings "buffer is empty" (reading from an empty buffer)
# and "buffer is full" (writing to a full one).
type pub CircularBuffer[T] {}

